  "solution": "__**Calculation:**__\n\n \n\nGiven,\n\nSet **A** = { 3, 5, 7, 9, 11 }\n\nSet **B** = { 7, 9, 11, 13 }\n\nSet **C** = { 11, 13, 15 }\n\nTo find the **Union** of sets **B** and **C**,\n\nB ∪ C = { 7, 9, 11, 13 } ∪ { 11, 13, 15 }\n\n⇒ B ∪ C = { 7, 9, 11, 13, 15 }\n\nNow, find the **Intersection** of **A** with (B ∪ C),\n\nA ∩ (B ∪ C) = { 3, 5, 7, 9, 11 } ∩ { 7, 9, 11, 13, 15 }\n\n⇒ A ∩ (B ∪ C) = { 7, 9, 11 }\n\n**∴ The resulting set is { 7, 9, 11 }.**",
